1. Start with the node

An AVL node needs:
  data
  pointer to left child
  pointer to right child
  height

struct Node {
    int data;
    struct Node *left;
    struct Node *right;
    int height;
};

Why height?
Because we need it to calculate:
  Balance Factor = height(left) - height(right)


2. Get the height

int height(struct Node *node)
{
    if (node == NULL)
        return 0;

    return node->height;
}

So:
NULL → height 0
And for a real node, we return its stored height.

3. Maximum function

When updating height, we'll need the larger of the two child heights.

int max(int a, int b)
{
    return (a > b) ? a : b;
}

Create a new node
struct Node* createNode(int data)
{
    struct Node *newNode = (struct Node*)malloc(sizeof(struct Node));

    newNode->data = data;
    newNode->left = NULL;
    newNode->right = NULL;
    newNode->height = 1;

    return newNode;
}
